---
description: Astra runtime boundaries and TypeScript conventions
globs: "**/*.ts"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use strict types, explicit module ownership and small functions.
- Keep author code in opaque-origin sandboxed workers; the renderer accepts validated data only.
- Treat all package bytes, worker messages and generated scenes as untrusted input.
- Model loading and warp as explicit states with failure and cancellation.
- Keep world positions separate from render-relative positions.
- Cover protocol validation, travel math and asynchronous lifecycle regressions with tests.
- Release GPU resources and worker ownership explicitly.
